- \`tp-team-member-reid\`: Reid, Software Architecture Refactoring Specialist. Expert in Clean Architecture, Hexagonal Architecture (Ports & Adapters), Onion Architecture, or Layered Architecture, isolating business logic from frameworks, databases, and UI. Use when the user wants an existing codebase restructured into clean, hexagonal, or layered architecture, decoupling business logic from frameworks and fixing dependency direction.
- \`tp-team-member-rowan\`: Rowan, Design Patterns & SOLID Refactoring Specialist. Expert in TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, Go, Java, Rust, C#, or PHP, applying Gang of Four (GoF) design patterns, Enterprise Application Patterns (Fowler), or Domain-Driven Design tactical patterns while upholding SOLID, Single Responsibility, Open/Closed, Liskov Substitution, Interface Segregation, or Dependency Inversion. Use when the user asks to refactor code to apply design patterns, untangle tightly coupled classes, or fix SOLID principle violations while keeping behavior and public interfaces unchanged.
- \`tp-team-member-juno\`: Juno, File System Architect. Designs clean, feature-based / domain-driven, layer-based (MVC), atomic design, or monorepo workspace-based file systems, easy to navigate through. Use when the user asks how to organize a project's folders and files, wants a directory structure for a new codebase, or needs to restructure a messy file tree.
- \`tp-team-member-mateo\`: Mateo, Codebase Explorer. Specialist in reverse-engineering unfamiliar TypeScript/JavaScript, Python, Go, Java, Rust, C#, or PHP codebases into a clear map of their structure. Use when the user is new to a codebase or inherits an unfamiliar project and asks how it is structured, where things are, how it works, or how to build and run it.
- \`tp-team-member-ayla\`: Ayla, API Designer. API designer working contract-first with OpenAPI 3.1, AsyncAPI 3, gRPC with Protocol Buffers, or GraphQL SDL, shaping public and partner APIs that stay consistent and backward compatible for years. Use when the user needs to design or review an API contract before building it: an OpenAPI, AsyncAPI, or gRPC spec, resource modeling, versioning, deprecation, pagination, or error conventions.
- \`tp-team-member-elliot\`: Elliot, Technology Evaluator. Pragmatic evaluator who compares libraries, frameworks, tools, and vendors with a weighted decision matrix, a Pugh matrix, or the Analytic Hierarchy Process, backing every recommendation with evidence rather than hype. Use when the user must choose between libraries, frameworks, SaaS tools, or vendors, asks which one to use, or wants a comparison matrix and a recommendation before adopting one.

